      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "bare_callee_in_pipe_position_is_unchanged",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  ],
  reason: "WHY THE EVIDENCE IS RUST TODAY: it was written before a .dag witness could reach this subject, and it stays only until an equivalent enrolled .dag witness is ported -- NOT because the floor cannot execute one. THE HISTORICAL REASON, KEPT AS HISTORY: this row was authored on the premise that it was a REACHABILITY limit rather than a preference: the two builtins a .dag witness would use for this subject -- compile_dag_rust_emit_check and compile_dag_diagnostic_census -- both resolve their synthetic source through v1_compiler.cli_run build_module_path_index_from_witness_roots, which walks the live tree. A witness written on either declares ReadsLiveTree. CORRECTED 2026-10-04, AND THE ORIGINAL SENTENCE IS QUOTED BECAUSE IT MISLED A READER: this row said such a witness 'is therefore DECLINED by the required floor's home policy rather than executed ... discovered, counted, and answering nothing'. That is no longer true. v2.workflow.required_floor deleted the DeclinedLiveTree arm (its own annotation records why: hermetic mode admits readonly checkout reads as input), so a ReadsLiveTree witness is routed and executed like any other identity. A compile_dag_diagnostic_census RED that reads its forged source from the checkout is therefore an enrollable witness. So the reachability limit that justified Rust here is gone: a .dag witness for this subject is now enrollable, and porting this evidence to one is this row's open next step, not a reason it lives in Rust. compile_sources takes its sources in memory, so the evidence here reads no repository file and needs no module index -- it is hermetic by construction, and it executes today under cargo test.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM: cargo test is a LOCAL check in this repository, removed from CI by operator ruling 2026-07-11. So this evidence executes on demand and is not a merge gate, and no gate closes this class until the enrolled .dag witness this row's trigger names exists and runs on the required floor. Stating that here rather than letting the row imply CI coverage is the point of writing it down.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE -- does the change serve the v2 self-host program. Under namespace-only resolution every callee becomes qualified, so a qualified callee in pipe position moves from rare to ordinary; the branch measured this class at roughly 119 of its 410 diagnostics. A parser that answers one denotation two ways by position is a direct tax on that program.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +7, all seven citable above and enumerated rather than counted, all seven in the ONE new file. src/v1/02_parse.dag is a .dag change and adds no hand item; its Rust mirror is generated, so its disposition is generated-surface regeneration and listing it would net a generated change into a hand census.\n\nA PARAGRAPH WAS REMOVED FROM THIS ROW AND THE REMOVAL IS RECORDED RATHER THAN MADE SILENTLY, because a census receipt that quietly changes what it claims is worse than one that was wrong once. An earlier revision of this row excluded six declarations in src/v1/stage0/src/bin/infer_semantics_witness.rs -- empty_type_env and five optional-match and resolve probes -- as ExistingSeedItemModified, each having gained one authored_import_names initializer. THAT PARAGRAPH IS NOW FALSE AND IS DELETED: the file has NO diff in this change, and origin/main already carries all six initializers. Main repaired them independently, and this branch's copy of the repair was dropped when a merge produced the field TWICE per literal -- main added it after module_path, this branch after source_visible_names, and git's text merge kept both (E0062 at six sites). Keeping main's placement removed this change's delta in that file entirely. So the exclusion paragraph described BASE-BRANCH work as part of this change, which makes a hand-Rust census receipt inaccurate in the one direction that matters -- it inflates what the change is answerable for. Found by review 56100.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE EVIDENCE, since the deleted paragraph also carried a live fact: the enumerated evidence could not execute at all while those six initializers were missing, because cargo builds a crate's bins for a --test target too. It executes now. The repair that made it executable is MAIN's, not this change's, and saying so is the point of correcting the row rather than deleting the sentence.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all seven when an enrolled .dag witness proves the same four cases through the compile builtins -- compile_dag_diagnostic_census or compile_dag_rust_emit_check over a probe source under dag/test/probe/, importing a fixture module where a qualified callee needs one, with a control that only names the modules -- and executes on the required floor. That capability exists now: v2.workflow.required_floor deleted DeclinedLiveTree, so a ReadsLiveTree witness runs, and a probe source compiled through the census may import other modules, so no further multi-module capability is owed. HISTORY, NOT A STANDING CONDITION: this trigger used to name a required phase compiling a multi-module closure from fixture-authored sources, and to say a witness on the single-source builtins would be declined; the decline no longer exists. What does NOT dissolve them is this defect being fixed -- the fix is what they guard.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_rhs; src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_callee_rest; src/v1/02_parse.dag pipe_callee_path_is_applied; src/v1/stage0/tests/qualified_callee_pipe_position.rs; dag/gunbc/qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth.dag"
}
